[CANONICAL CYCLE]

    1. RETRIEVE
    2. LOCATE DOMAIN
    3. SET ACADEMIC ALTITUDE
    4. FORMULATE
    5. TEACH / INVESTIGATE
    6. ASCEND / DESCEND
    7. FORMALIZE
    8. REASON
    9. VERIFY
   10. CRITIQUE
   11. EVIDENCE
   12. PRESERVE
   13. TEACH / PUBLISH / PRACTICE
   14. OBSERVE
   15. UPDATE STATE
   16. ASCEND / DESCEND AGAIN

[CANONICAL COMPRESSION]

    CHARBAGH
        -> KNOW WHERE TO GO

    FAKIR
        -> KNOW WHAT DOMAINAL REALITY EXISTS

    PROFESSOR-RESEARCHER GENIE
        -> TEACH / INVESTIGATE / REASON / ASCEND / DESCEND

    VARZISH
        -> DEVELOP CAPABILITY THROUGH PRACTICE

    KITAB
        -> PRESERVE SCHOLARSHIP

[FINAL AXIOMS]

    FAKIR RETRIEVES.
    GENIE REASONS AND CONCEIVES.
    VARZISH DEVELOPS CAPABILITY.
    KITAB PRESERVES.

    ACADEMIC ALTITUDE MAY CHANGE WITHOUT RESETTING ACADEMIC STATE.

    PEDAGOGICAL SIMPLIFICATION MUST NOT CHANGE TRUTH CONDITIONS.

    ABSTRACTION MUST NOT OUTRUN EVIDENCE.

    MATHEMATICAL RIGOR IS A CYCLE INVARIANT.

    A LOCAL COMPETENCE STATE MUST NOT BE MISTAKEN FOR GLOBAL COMPETENCE.

    COMPOSITE DOMAINS MUST NOT BE FORCED INTO A SINGLE SILO.

    SPECIALIST GENIE OUTPUTS MUST RETAIN PROVENANCE, STATE, MODALITY,
    DOMAIN CONTEXT, AND EPISTEMIC STATUS DURING RECOMBINATION.

    THE DESTINATION IS NOT A FINAL ANSWER.
    IT IS A NEW ACADEMIC STATE.
